# Docker build context for the Dockerfile at the repo root. ALLOW-LIST: everything is excluded, then only the
# files the image needs are let back in. This keeps secrets (.env), downloaded data (data/), local caches
# (.venv, node_modules, .cache, qdrant_storage), results/ and the git history out of the build context.

# 1. Exclude everything.
*

# 2. Let back in what the Dockerfile copies. The eval/ and results/ entries are the Lender Desk demo's SYNTHETIC
#    applications and the screening threshold; the first two scripts download the public lists and build the guideline
#    index at build time (stage "assets"); the third builds the real metros' Studio snapshots when the build has the
#    Census key secret (stage "studio-snapshots"). Nothing else under eval/, results/, scripts/ or data/ comes back.
!pyproject.toml
!uv.lock
!README.md
!src/
!config/
!corpus/
!frontend/
!eval/applications/
!eval/startup_applications/
!results/kyc_metrics.json
!scripts/download_data.py
!scripts/build_index.py
!scripts/build_studio_snapshots.py

# 3. Inside those folders, exclude build output, dependencies, caches and anything secret-looking.
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/.DS_Store
frontend/node_modules
frontend/.next
frontend/out
frontend/*.tsbuildinfo
frontend/next-env.d.ts
frontend/npm-debug.log*
# Frontend dev helpers that are not part of the build (screenshots need Python + Playwright; the mock API and its
# recorded fixtures serve the pages without a backend).
frontend/scripts/screenshots.py
frontend/scripts/screenshots_mock.py
frontend/scripts/record_mock_fixtures.py
frontend/mock-api
